# Faillock preauth profile (check-and-lock BEFORE the primary auth module).
# Managed by Ansible - ssh_2fa role.
#
# WHY TWO PROFILES: pam_faillock(8) requires `preauth` to run BEFORE pam_unix and
# `authfail`/`authsucc` AFTER it. pam-auth-update orders Primary profiles by
# Priority (higher = earlier). The unix (pam_unix) profile is Priority 256, so
# this preauth profile at 1024 renders ahead of it and the companion `faillock`
# profile at Priority 0 renders after it -> preauth / pam_unix / authfail/authsucc.
# The previous single Priority-900 profile put ALL faillock lines before pam_unix,
# which degrades the failure tally (the audit's flagged common-auth anomaly).
#
# CHANGE CONTROL: this edits the LIVE common-auth stack. Do NOT converge blind —
# render + verify in molecule/default first, and on prod hold a root session +
# Hetzner console open and confirm `pamtester login <user> authenticate` passes.
Name: Faillock preauth (account lockout check)
Default: yes
Priority: 1024
Auth-Type: Primary
Auth:
	requisite			pam_faillock.so preauth
Account-Type: Primary
Account:
	required			pam_faillock.so
